course: dictionary
lesson: 8341
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Romeo» can be a name, a word for a romantic young man, or a letter in the radio spelling alphabet. The words around it tell you which meaning is needed.
explain: In «William Shakespeare wrote plays such as Romeo and Juliet, Hamlet and Macbeth around 1600 for the Globe theatre in London», Romeo is the title of a play, so it is a name. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Informal means casual, everyday talk, not formal writing. If someone says, «he thinks he's a real Romeo», they mean a young man who flirts a lot. A capital letter, a play title, or a spelling of letters is another clue.
fact: Romeo is a boy's name.
fact: The most famous Romeo is the young lover in Shakespeare's play «Romeo and Juliet».
fact: «Romeo» (informal) means a young man who flirts a lot or acts like a romantic lover.
fact: In the NATO spelling alphabet, «Romeo» stands for the letter R.
fact: Shakespeare wrote «Romeo and Juliet» around 1600 for the Globe theatre in London.
exercise: In «Romeo and Juliet», what kind of word is Romeo? | A word for a flirty young man | A type of petrol station | A letter of the alphabet | *A name
exercise: Ruby says, «He thinks he's a real Romeo.» What does Romeo mean here? | A petrol station | The letter R | *A young man who flirts a lot or acts like a romantic lover | A famous playwright
exercise: A pilot says «Romeo» over the radio to spell a letter. What letter is it? | O | *R | Q | J
test: Which letter does «Romeo» stand for in the radio spelling alphabet? | B | M | *R | T
test: In the sentence «He thinks he's a real Romeo», is Romeo a name or an informal word? | A name | A letter of the alphabet | *An informal word for a flirty young man | A place in London
exam: In «Shakespeare wrote Romeo and Juliet», which meaning of Romeo fits? | The letter R | A famous writer | A young man who flirts a lot | *A name, the title character of a play
